  <page>
    <title>Efke</title>
    <id>176085</id>
    <revision>
      <id>40499340</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-21T00:26:12Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Rich Farmbrough</username>
        <id>82835</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>External links per MoS.</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">[[Image:KB25.JPG|right]]
'''Efke''' is the brand name of [[photographic film|films]], [[photographic paper|photo papers]], and chemicals manufactured by ''Fotokemika d.d.'', a company located in [[Samobor]], [[Croatia]].

==Products specification==

The Efke films are &quot;old-school&quot; [[emulsion]]s with very high [[silver]] content and as a result give a large [[exposure (photography)|exposure]] latitude and superior grayscale reproduction. The Efke 25, 50 and 100 products are made using the [[ADOX]] formulas that were first introduced in the [[1950s]].

Unlike many modern black and white films the Efke products are true to their rated speed and unlike modern tabular crystal films, which are very unforgiving to use, even beginners can produce quality images. The nature of the product also easily allows large, grain free, enlargements to be made from negatives.

Efke films are coated in one layer, unlike most other films which are coated in multiple layers.

==External links==
*[http://www.efkeusa.com Efke Film]
*[http://www.efke.hr Efke website (doesn't seem to have any info on film)]

[[Category:Brands]]
[[Category:Companies of Croatia]]</text>
    </revision>
