      <text xml:space="preserve">:''Note that the acronym [[ANS]] stands for several items; see its page.''
-----
'''Ans''' is a [[municipality]] located in the [[Belgium|Belgian]] province of [[Liege (province)|Li&amp;egrave;ge]]. On January 1st, 2005 Ans had a total population of 27,350. The total area is 23.35 [[square kilometre|km&amp;sup2;]] which gives a [[population density]] of 1,171.19 inhabitants per km&amp;sup2;.

Ans is also the finish location of the famous [[road bicycle racing|road bicycle race]] [[Liège-Bastogne-Liège]], the oldest of the [[classic cycle races]].

==External links==
*[http://www.ans-commune.be/ Official website ] - Only available in [[French language|French]]

