      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Esneux''' is a [[municipality]] located in the [[Belgium|Belgian]] province of [[Liege (province)|Li&amp;egrave;ge]]. On [[January 1]] [[2005]] Esneux had a total population of 13,167. The total area is 34.05 [[square kilometre|km&amp;sup2;]] which gives a [[population density]] of 386.74 inhabitants per km&amp;sup2;.

Esneux is constituted of a series of villages : Esneux, Mery, Hony and Tilff. They are all to be found in the valley of the [[Ourthe]] river south of [[Liège (city)|Li&amp;egrave;ge]]. A railway line links the 4 villages (and then continues further south to [[Luxemburg]]).

