        <username>Textex</username>
        <id>605657</id>
      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">The foregoing list of '''Famous trains''' primarily includes those [[Rail transport|train routes]] that have come to be considered &quot;legendary&quot; both in recent times and during their past history. Before the post-World War II period with the advent of more democratised [[Scheduled air transport|air transport]], rail travel was the predominant means of [[transport|transportation]] for long-distance travel--and was therefore most common only for the wealthy or those with an urgent personal or business need. Since the late [[20th century]], the main purpose of the majority of these [[Rail transport|trains]] is [[tourism]]. Nonetheless, certain routes are still integral parts of the transport systems of some countries (e.g. [[Russia]]).

* [[1848]] : [[Barcelona-Mataró]], ([[Barcelona]]) 
* [[1862]] : [[Flying Scotsman (train)|Flying Scotsman]]
* [[1883]] : [[Orient Express]] 
* [[1884]] : [[Nord Express]] (Northern Express)
* [[1887]] : [[Sud Express]] (Southern Express)
* [[1890]] : [[Bombay Express]] 
* [[1890]] : [[Peninsular and Oriental Express]]  
* [[1890]] : [[Malle des Indes]]  
* [[1890]] : [[Rome Express]]  
* [[1894]] : [[Ostend Vienna Express]]  
* [[1896]] : [[Vienna Nice Express]]  
* [[1898]] : [[Cairo Luxor Express]]  
* [[1898]] : [[Trans-Siberian Railway]]  
* [[1900]] : [[Riviera Express]]  
* [[1900]] : [[Transatlantic Express]]  
* [[1902]] : [[20th Century Limited]]
* [[1903]] : [[Yellow train]]
* [[1904]] : [[Oberland Leman Express]]
* [[1904]] : [[Ocean (passenger train)|Ocean Limited]]
* [[1908]] : [[Brighton Belle]] (formerly the Southern Belle)
* [[1908]] : [[Rome Florence Cannes Express]]  
* [[1909]] : [[Andalousie Express]]  
* [[1912]] : [[Broadway Limited]]
* [[1919]] : [[Paris Prague Express]]  
* [[1919]] : [[Orient Express|Simplon Orient Express]]  
* [[1921]] : [[Transmanchurian Express]]  
* [[1922]] : [[Blue Train (South Africa)|Blue Train]]  
* [[1926]] : [[Golden Arrow]] 
* [[1927]] : [[Northern Star (passenger train)|Northern Star]]  
* [[1927]] : [[London Vichy Pullman Express]]  
* [[1928]] : [[Frontier Mail]]
* [[1928]] : [[Rheingold Express]] (Rhine Gold)
* [[1929]] : [[Oiseau Bleu]]  
* [[1929]] : [[Côte d'Azur rapide]]  
* [[1929]] : [[Star of Egypt]]  
* [[1929]] : [[Taurus Express]]  
* [[1929]] : [[Sunshine Pullman Express]]  
* [[1929]] : [[The Ghan]]
* [[1929]] : [[The Grand Trunk Express]]
* [[1929]] : [[Empire Builder]]
* [[1931]] : [[Golden Mountain Express]] 
* [[1937]] : [[Super Chief]]
* [[1940]] : [[Maroc Express]]  
* [[1944]] : [[Armored train Štefánik]]
* [[1944]] : [[Armored train Hurban]]
* [[1947]] : [[City of New Orleans]]  
* [[1955]] : [[The Canadian]]  
* [[1960]]s : [[Master Cutler]]
* [[1964]] : [[Shinkansen]]
* [[1970]] : [[Indian Pacific]]
* [[2000]]s : [[Eurostar]]

* [[Russian Railways]] ([[Russia]] and the [[USSR|Soviet Union]])
** [[Rossiya (train)|Rossiya]], operated on the [[Trans-Siberian railway]]
** [[Nikolayevski Express]] operated between [[Moscow]] and [[Saint Petersburg]]
* Zephyr trains ([[United States]])
:* [[1934]]: [[Pioneer Zephyr]]
:* [[1949]]: [[California Zephyr]]
:* [[Minnesota Zephyr]]
:* [[Nebraska Zephyr]]

[[Category:Named passenger trains]]

[[de:Luxuszug]]
[[fr:Liste de trains célèbres]]
[[nl:Beroemde spoorlijnen en treinen]]</text>
    </revision>
