  <page>
    <title>AP (disambiguation)</title>
    <id>176123</id>
    <revision>
      <id>41617620</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-28T15:28:47Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Kbdank71</username>
        <id>197953</id>
      </contributor>
      <comment>per [[WP:CFD]] [[Wikipedia:Categories for deletion/Log/2006 February 20|Feb 20]] using [[Wikipedia:AutoWikiBrowser|AWB]]</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''AP''', '''Ap''', or '''ap''' may mean:
* [[Associated Press]], an American [[news agency]]
* [[Accounts payable]], an accounting term
* [[Access Point]], provides multipoint access for wireless broadband connections from [[SU]].
* [[Action potential]], an electrical event in the [[neuron]]
* [[Advanced Placement Program]], a [[College Board]] [[high school]] program
* [[Air One]] IATA code
* [[Andhra Pradesh]], a state in [[south India]]
* Andean Pact, now the [[Andean Community]], a trade agreement
* Atos Prime, one of the [[Hyundai Atos]] cars
* [[Wireless access point]], similar to a hub used in [[Ethernet]] networking but using wireless technologies
* [[Acetone peroxide]], an explosive
* ''[[Amiga Power]]'',  a defunct monthly [[computer magazine]] about [[Amiga]] computer games
* ''[[Popular Action (Peru)]]'' (&quot;Acción Popular&quot;), a political party
* AP, the U.S. military [[U.S. postal abbreviations|state code]] for personnel in the Pacific Ocean region
* AP, the U.S. Navy [[hull classification symbol]] for &quot;transport&quot;
* [[School principal|Assistant principal]]
* [[Arithmetic progression]], a sequence of numbers, each differing from its predecessor by a fixed quantity
* [[Armor-piercing shot and shell]]
* Ap, a nickname for the comic book character [[Apathy Kat]]
* Ap, the [[Welsh language|Welsh]] [[patronymic]], corresponding to Gaelic ''mac''.  For example, [[Dafydd ap Gruffydd]]
* [[Aap|Ap]] or Aap, the Hindu term for water as a classical element and a diefied personification thereof. 
* [[A&amp;P]] grocery store
* [[Au pair]]

{{2CC}}

