      <text xml:space="preserve">{{dablink|This article is not about the character in Anne Rice's The Vampire Chronicles; see [[Amel (fictional character)]]}}
{{dablink|For the river see [[Amel (river)]]}}
{{dablink|For part of Lebanon or Palestine see [[Jabal Amel]]}}


'''Amel''' ([[French language|French]]: ''Ambl&amp;egrave;ve'') is a [[municipality]] in the [[Belgium|Belgian]] province of [[Liege (province)|Li&amp;egrave;ge]], and is part of the [[German speaking community in Belgium|Deutschsprachige Gemeinschaft Belgien]].

On [[January 1]] [[2005]] Amel had a total population of 5,255. The total area is 125.15 [[square kilometre|km&amp;sup2;]] which gives a [[population density]] of 41.99 inhabitants per km&amp;sup2;.
There are seventeen villages in Amel: Schoppen, Stephanshof, Iveldingen, Eibertingen, Montenau, Born, Deidenberg, Medell, M&amp;ouml;derscheid, Hepscheid, Heppenbach, Halenfeld, Mirfeld, Valender, Wereth, Meyerode, and Herresbach.

&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;

[[Category:Municipalities of Liège]]
[[Category:Cities and towns in Belgium]]
