      <text xml:space="preserve">[[Image:Aubel JPG01.jpg|thumb|right|256px|Aubel: the village centre]]
'''Aubel''' is a [[municipality]] located in the [[Belgium|Belgian]] province of [[Liege (province)|Li&amp;egrave;ge]]. On [[1 January]] [[2005]] the municipality had 4,056 inhabitants (1,989 males and 2,067 females). The total area is 18.83 [[square kilometre|km&amp;sup2;]], giving a [[population density]] of 215.4 inhabitants per km&amp;sup2;.

Aubel is famous for its butchers, cheesemakers, and cider and beer breweries. An open-air market is held in the centre of Aubel every Sunday morning. This market has been in continuous weekly existence since [[1630]].

