        <id>718098</id>
      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">[[Image:Eupen-Nicolas-Church.JPG|thumb|St Nikolaus church in Eupen]]
'''Eupen''' is a [[municipality]] located in the [[Belgium|Belgian]] province of [[Liege (province)|Li&amp;egrave;ge]], 10 miles from the German border ([[Aachen]]), from the Dutch border ([[Maastricht]]) and from the nature reservation &quot;Hohes Venn&quot; ([[Ardennes]]). 


On January 1st, 2005 Eupen had a total population of 18,038 (8,769 males and 9,269 females). The total area is 103.74 [[square kilometre|km&amp;sup2;]] which gives a [[population density]] of 173.88 inhabitants per km&amp;sup2;.

At the end of the First World War, Eupen and neighboring [[Malmedy]] districts were subject to a plebiscite to determine whether the region would be separated from Germany and annexed to Belgium.  The plebiscite ballots required names and postal addresses of the voters.  Fearing deportation, the populations of Eupen and Malmedy voted to join Belgium.

Eupen is the seat of the Council of the [[German speaking community in Belgium]] and the official language in Eupen is [[German language|German]], although [[Dutch language|Dutch]] was widely spoken in Eupen in the 18th century. There is also a small University College in Eupen, the [[Autonome Hochschule in der deutschsprachigen Gemeinschaft]], offering bachelor degrees in Education and Nursing.


==External links==
* [http://www.eupen.be Official Homepage]
*[http://www.eupen-info.be Tourist Info]
{{commons|Eupen|Eupen}}

{{belgium-geo-stub}}

