      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Kelmis''' (in French, '''La Calamine''') is a [[municipality]] located in the [[Belgium|Belgian]] province of [[Liege (province)|Li&amp;egrave;ge]]. On [[January 1]] [[2005]] Kelmis had a total population of 10,249. The total area is 18.12 [[square kilometre|km&amp;sup2;]] which gives a [[population density]] of 565.56 inhabitants per km&amp;sup2;.

The territory around the [[Vieille Montagne]] [[zinc]] mine in Kelmis was semi-independent during [[1816]]-[[1919]] as '''Neutral [[Moresnet]]'''.

