      <text xml:space="preserve">[[Image:BurgRaeren02.jpg|thumb|200px]]'''Raeren''' is a [[municipality]] located in the [[Belgium|Belgian]] province of [[Liege (province)|Li&amp;egrave;ge]]. It was part of Germany until the [[First World War]], after which it became part of Belgium. It is one of several towns in Eastern Belgium which still predominantly speak German.

On [[January 1]] [[2005]] Raeren had a total population of 9,945. The total area is 74.21 [[square kilometre|km&amp;sup2;]] which gives a [[population density]] of 134.00 inhabitants per km&amp;sup2;.

== See also ==
