      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Hannut''' is a [[municipality]] located in the [[Belgium|Belgian]] province of [[Liege (province)|Li&amp;egrave;ge]]. On [[January 1]] [[2005]] Hannut had a total population of 14,085. The total area is 86.53 [[square kilometre|km&amp;sup2;]] which gives a [[population density]] of 162.77 inhabitants per km&amp;sup2;.

Seventeen villages are included in the greater Hannut area: 
Abolens, Avernas-le-Bauduin, Avin, Bertrée, Blehen, Cras-Avernas, Crehen, Grand-Hallet, Lens-Saint-Remy, Merdorp, Moxhe, Petit-Hallet, Poucet, Thisnes, Trognée, Villers-le-Peuplier, and Wansin. 

The Battle of Hannut, which began May 12, 1940, is credited with being the first battle between tanks of World War II.

