  <page>
    <title>Dulong-Petit law</title>
    <id>176178</id>
    <revision>
      <id>41062982</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-24T20:44:50Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <ip>69.137.220.40</ip>
      </contributor>
      <comment>/* See also */</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">The '''Dulong-Petit law''' is a [[scientific law|chemical law]] proposed in [[1819]] by [[France|French]] [[chemists]] [[Pierre Louis Dulong]] and [[Alexis Thérèse Petit]], states the classical expression for the [[specific heat capacity]] of a [[crystal]] due to its [[phonon|lattice vibration]]s. 

The result is extremely simple; regardless of the nature of the crystal, the specific heat capacity (measured in joule per kelvin per kilogram) is equal to 3''R''/''MM'', where ''R'' is the [[gas constant]] (measured in joule per kelvin per mole) and ''MM'' is the [[molar mass]] (measured in kilogram per mole). In other words, the [[Heat capacity#Dimensionless heat capacity|dimensionless heat capacity]] is equal to 3.

Despite its simplicity, Dulong-Petit law offers fairly good prediction for the specific heat capacity of solids with relatively simple crystal structure at high [[temperature]]s. It fails, however, in the low temperature region, where the quantum mechanical nature of the solid manifests itself. There, the [[Debye model]] works well.

the Dulong Petit Law states that the specific heat capacity for solids is = 3 NR


==See also==
*[[Stefan-Boltzmann law]]

[[Category:Condensed matter physics]]
[[Category:Eponymous laws]]
[[Category:Thermodynamics]]

[[de:Dulong-Petit-Gesetz]]
[[fr:Loi de Dulong et Petit]]
[[ja:デュロン＝プティの法則]]</text>
    </revision>
  </page>
  <page>
    <title>Arlon</title>
    <id>176180</id>
    <revision>
      <id>39644531</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-14T22:15:24Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <ip>213.5.28.248</ip>
      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">[[Image:arlon-stmartin1.jpg|thumbnail|190px|right| St Martin church, Arlon ]]

'''Arlon''' ([[Dutch language|Dutch]]: ''Aarlen'', [[German language|German]]: ''Arel'') is a [[municipality]] located in the [[Belgium|Belgian]] province of [[Luxembourg (province of Belgium)|Luxembourg]], of which it is the capital. On January 1st, 2005 Arlon had a total population of 25,986. The total area is 118.64 [[square kilometre|km&amp;sup2;]] which gives a [[population density]] of 219.04 inhabitants per km&amp;sup2;.  Arlon is twinned with [[Saint-Dié-des-Vosges|Saint-Dié-des-Vosges]] (France), [[Diekirch|Dieckirch]] (Grand-Duchy of Luxembourg) [[Bitburg|Bitburg]] (Germany twinned since 1965), [[Sulphur, Louisiana|Sulphur]] (USA), [[Hayange|Hayange]] (France), [[Alba, Italy|Alba]] (Italy) and [[Market Drayton]] (United Kingdom).

The local tipple of Maitrank (made from white wine, Cognac and woodruff) is celebrated with its own festival each May.  


==Gallery==

&lt;gallery&gt;

Image:Arlon JPG01.jpg|St. Donat church (XVIIth century).
Image:Arlon JPG02.jpg|Roofs of the city and St. Martin bell tower.
Image:Arlon JPG03.jpg|Way of the Cross with his stone stations.
Image:Arlon JPG04.jpg|St. Donat church and top of the Way of the Cross.

&lt;/gallery&gt;


== External link ==
*[http://www.arlon.be/ Official website of Arlon city]

