      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Durbuy''' is a [[municipality]] located in the [[Belgium|Belgian]] province of [[Luxembourg (province of Belgium)|Luxembourg]]. On [[January 1]] [[2005]] Durbuy had a total population of 10,374. The total area is 156.61 [[square kilometre|km&amp;sup2;]] which gives a [[population density]] of 66.24 inhabitants per km&amp;sup2;.

In medieval times Durbuy was an important centre of commerce and industry. In [[1331]] the town was elevated to the rank of [[city]] by [[John I, Count of Luxemburg]], and King of Bohemia. 

Durbuy is the smallest city of [[Europe]], and probably of the world. Tourism and recreation are its main activities nowadays.

[[Category:Municipalities of Luxembourg (Belgium)]]
