  <page>
    <title>La Roche-en-Ardenne</title>
    <id>176199</id>
    <revision>
      <id>32537171</id>
      <timestamp>2005-12-23T23:28:16Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <ip>213.189.163.61</ip>
      </contributor>
      <comment>lb:</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''La Roche-en-Ardenne''' is a [[municipality]] located in the [[Belgium|Belgian]] province of [[Luxembourg (province of Belgium)|Luxembourg]]. On [[January 1]] [[2005]] La Roche-en-Ardenne had a total population of 4,201. The total area is 147.52 [[square kilometre|km&amp;sup2;]] which gives a [[population density]] of 28.48 inhabitants per km&amp;sup2;.

Situated by a curve of the river [[Ourthe]], the small town of La Roche-en-Ardenne is one of the more popular tourist destinations in the [[Ardennes]].
Walking, kayaking and mountain-biking are among the popular outdoor activities in the area.

Apart from tourism, the other principal activity in the municipality is agriculture.

==History==
La Roche is believed to have first been settled in the [[Neolithic]] era.
The [[Ancient Rome|Romans]] built a fort there following their conquest of Gaul and the Ardennes. 

The town's medieval castle was in use between the [[9th century|9th]] and [[18th century|18th]] centuries.

In [[World War II]], the town suffered severe damage. Having been liberated by the [[Allies of World War II|Allies]] in September [[1944]], the town was recaptured by the [[Nazi Germany|Germans]] in December, during the [[Battle of the Bulge]]. The subsequent Allied bombing raids resulted in the town being liberated once more in January [[1945]], but left much of the town destroyed, and many residents dead.


==References==
* [http://www.la-roche-tourisme.com/uk/histoire-frame.htm History of La Roche]
* [http://www.taipeitimes.com/News/world/archives/2004/12/10/2003214500 AP news report on the 60th anniversary of the Battle of the Bulge]

==External links==
* [http://www.la-roche-en-ardenne.be/ Municipality website]


{{belgium-geo-stub}}

[[Category:Municipalities of Luxembourg (Belgium)]]

