      <text xml:space="preserve">[[Image:Marche-en-Famenne JPG01.jpg|thumb|right|The St. Remacle Church.|200px]]
'''Marche-en-Famenne''' is a [[municipality]] located in the [[Belgium|Belgian]] province of [[Luxembourg (province of Belgium)|Luxembourg]]. On [[January 1]] [[2005]] Marche-en-Famenne had a total population of 16,779. The total area is 121.40 [[square kilometre|km&amp;sup2;]] which gives a [[population density]] of 138.21 inhabitants per km&amp;sup2;.

In [[1977]], Marche-en-Famenne was merged with the villages of [[Aye]], [[Hargimont]], [[Humain]], [[On, Belgium|On]], [[Roy, Belgium|Roy]], [[Waha]], and [[Marloie]].

