      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Libin''' is a [[municipality]] located in the [[Belgium|Belgian]] province of [[Luxembourg (province of Belgium)|Luxembourg]]. On [[January 1]] [[2005]] Libin had a total population of 4,564. The total area is 139.72 [[square kilometre|km&amp;sup2;]] which gives a [[population density]] of 32.66 inhabitants per km&amp;sup2;.

Other than the central town of Libin, the municipality includes the villages of Anloy, Ochamps, Redu, Smuid, Transinne and Villance.

Redu is famous for its book stores, as well as for hosting a large [[European Space Agency]] ground site.

