      <contributor>
        <username>Zinneke</username>
        <id>574691</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>lb:</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">:''For the town in France, see [[Neufchâteau, Vosges]].''

'''Neufchâteau''' ([[Walloon language|Walloon]]: Li Tchestea) is a [[municipality]] located in the central part of the [[Belgium|Belgian]] province of [[Luxembourg (province of Belgium)|Luxembourg]].

On [[January 2005|January 1st, 2005]] Neufch&amp;acirc;teau had a total population of 6,379. The total area is 113.79 [[square kilometre|km&amp;sup2;]] which gives a [[population density]] of 56.06 inhabitants per km&amp;sup2;.

*[[List of postal codes in Belgium|Postal code]]: 6840 (6620)

Between [[1795]] and [[1815]], it was the chief town of the old French ''département'' of [[Forêts]]. During the First World War its governor, Count Hans [[von Blumenthal]], was one of a small number of German military officials who struck up a rapport with the local population, chiefly through his interest in hunting.

[[Image:Neufchâteau JPG02.jpg|thumb|right|'''Neufchâteau''', the hall of justice.|250px]]

==Villages==

*[[Grandvoir]] (Walloon: Grandwar)
*[[Grapfontaine]] (Walloon: Grapfontinne)
*[[Hamipré]] (Walloon: Hamîpré)
*[[Longlier]] (Walloon: Longuié)
*[[Tournay (Neufchâteau)|Tournay]]

==Historical population==

