      <text xml:space="preserve">&lt;table align=&quot;right&quot;&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td&gt;
[[Image:Chiny-blason.jpg|Entry of the Orval via the guest house.]] 
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;

'''Chiny''' is a [[municipality]] located in the [[Belgium|Belgian]] province of [[Luxembourg (province of Belgium)|Luxembourg]] and the [[Gaume]] region. On January 1st, 2005 Chiny had a total population of 4,966. The total area is 113.69 [[square kilometre|km&amp;sup2;]] which gives a [[population density]] of 43.68 inhabitants per km&amp;sup2;.

[[Chiny]] is located in the south of the [[French language|French]]-speaking region. The municipality is on the boundary between  the region of [[Gaume]] and the [[Ardennes]].

Six villages are in the municipality of Chiny :

* Chiny
* Izel   
* Jamoigne   
* [[Les Bulles]] 
* Suxy  
* Termes

The [[blazon]] of the municipality is composed of three silver [[trout]] with a blue background color.

On a historical perspective, [[Chiny]] is an old county and was larger than the current municipality.

==External link ==
*[http://www.chiny.be/ Official web site of the municipality]

