      <text xml:space="preserve">[[Image:Virton JPG01.jpg|thumb|right|288px|Virton: St Lawrence's church]]
'''Virton''' is the most southerly town in [[Belgium]] and the administrative centre of a municipality (''commune'') and district (''arrondissement'') of the same name, located in the [[Belgium|Belgian]] province of [[Luxembourg (province of Belgium)|Luxembourg]]. 

On [[1 January]] [[2005]] the municipality had 11,106 inhabitants (5,387 males and 5,719 females). The total area is 94.49 [[square kilometre|km&amp;sup2;]], giving a [[population density]] of 117.54 inhabitants per km&amp;sup2;. Virton is the principal town of the small region of [[Belgian Lorraine]] known as the [[Gaume]], famous for its [[microclimate]].

==External links==
