  <page>
    <title>Farrah</title>
    <id>176233</id>
    <revision>
      <id>41777781</id>
      <timestamp>2006-03-01T18:00:42Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <ip>87.74.63.225</ip>
      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">{{Infobox_band |
  band_name         = Farrah|
  years_active      = [[1999]]&amp;ndash;present |
  country           = [[London]], [[England]] |
  music_genre       = [[Power_pop|Power Pop]] |
  record_label      = [[Lojinx]] |
  current_members   = Jez Ashurst&lt;br /&gt;Andrew Campbell&lt;br /&gt;Mike Hopkins&lt;br /&gt;Michelle Margherita|
}}

:''For the model and actress, see [[Farrah Fawcett]].  For other uses, see [[Farah]] (disambig)''
'''Farrah''' are a UK [[power pop]] quartet formed in the north east of [[England]] in [[1999]]. After releasing their debut single &quot;Terry&quot; on the [[independent record label|indie]] Noisebox label in the UK they were signed to [[The Police]] manager Miles Copland's [[Ark21]] label for the release of their debut album &quot;Moustache&quot;. The album was released in the UK, USA, Europe and Japan and saw the band tour the world extensively to support it.  Alas, the albums commercial failure bankrupted [[Ark21]] and in 2004 their 2nd album was released on various independent labels throughout the world.

Whilst developing a harder rock sound “me too” incorporated more diverse elements into their sound whilst still essentially remaining true to the lyrically quirky 3-minute harmony-laden melody-driven [[power pop]] format the band became known for.  

Although Farrah have built up a solid fan base over the years they have never crossed into the mainstream consciousness and remain largely unknown outside [[indie (music)|indie]] / [[power pop]] circles. The band are often cited alongside bands such as [[Fountains Of Wayne]] and [[Weezer]] as keepers of the contemporary [[power pop]] flame.

==Discography, albums==
[[Image:Lojinx_ljx003cd_thumb.jpg]] [[Image:Lojinx_ljx005cd_thumb.jpg]] [[Image:Farrah_SGP.gif]]
* [[2001]]: ''[[Moustache]]''
* [[2004]]: ''[[Me Too]]''
* [[2005]]: ''[[Stopgap Product]]'' (Japan only mini-album)

== Members ==
*Jez Ashurst - [[Vocals]], [[Guitar]], [[Keyboard instrument|Keyboards]]
*Andy Campbell - [[Guitar]], [[Keyboard instrument|Keyboards]], [[Vocals]]
*Mike Hopkins - [[Drums]], [[Vocals]]
*Michelle Margherita - [[Bass guitar]], [[Vocals]]

Past members include Tom Marsh (drums, of [[Repairman]]), Max Fidanni (drums) and Mike Walker (bass, founder member).

==External links==
* [http://www.farrah.co.uk Farrah Homepage]
* [[Ark21]] ([http://www.Ark21.com Ark21] (USA))
* [[Lojinx]] ([http://www.Lojinx.com Lojinx] (UK))
* [[Rock Indiana]] ([http://www.rockindiana.biz Rock Indiana] (Spain))
* [[Polaris]] ([http://www.polaris-musique.fr Polaris/MVS] (France))
* [[Egging]] ([http://www.1977records.com/ 1977/Egging] (Japan))

[[Category:English musical groups]]
[[Category:British musical groups]]</text>
    </revision>
  </page>
