      <contributor>
        <username>Blarneytherinosaur</username>
        <id>208823</id>
      </contributor>
      <comment>Presbyterian Inland Mission</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''PIM''' is an acronym for: 
* [[Platform-independent model]]
* [[Personal information manager]]
* Pilot's information manual
* [[Protocol Independent Multicast]]
* [[processor-in-memory]]
* [[Penalty minutes]] (hockey)
* [[Fifth generation computer systems project|Parallel inference machine]]
* [[Product information management]]
* [[Presbyterian Inland Mission]]

The word '''Pim''' can refer to:
* [[Pim Fortuyn]], an assassinated Dutch politician.

{{TLAdisambig}}</text>
    </revision>
  </page>
  <page>
    <title>Personal information manager</title>
    <id>176292</id>
    <revision>
      <id>40474437</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-20T20:51:27Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Quarl</username>
        <id>59118</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>Reverted edits by [[Special:Contributions/87.229.143.94|87.229.143.94]] ([[User talk:87.229.143.94|talk]]) to last version by Perfecto</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">A '''personal information manager''' ('''PIM''') is a type of [[application software]] that functions as a [[personal organizer]]. As an [[information management]] tool, a PIM's purpose is to facilitate the recording, tracking, and management of certain types of &quot;personal information&quot;, including personal notes, digital [[address book]]s, lists (including [[task list]]s), and significant [[calendar date]]s; some PIMs may also manage [[e-mail]] or [[fax]] communications, or boast [[project management]] features.

Some PIM software products are capable of synchronizing data with another PIM over a [[computer network]] (including [[mobile ad-hoc network]]s, or MANETs). This feature usually does not allow for continuous, concurrent data updates, but rather enables point-in-time updating between different computers, including [[desktop computer]]s, [[laptop]] computers, and [[personal digital assistant]]s).
PIM = e-mail, calendar and contacts - always updated directly on the mobilephone.
With a PIM software in combination with a smartphone or a pda, that is the reality. There is no longer a need to look for a wireless zone or a network connection in order to log on to the computer to access e-mails. With a PIM solution you're always up to date on your appointments and your e-mails - regardless of where you are or what you're doing.


==See also==
*[[Calendar]]
*[[Comparison of personal information managers]]
*[[Information management]]
*[[List of personal information managers]]
*[[Personal organizer]]


{{software-stub}}

[[Category:Personal information managers]]

[[de:Personal Information Management]]
[[it:Personal information manager]]
[[nl:Personal Information Manager]]
[[pl:PIM]]
[[sv:PIM]]</text>
