      <comment>/* Browser extensions */ +[[Wikipedia:Toolbars]] reference</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">{{shortcut|[[WP:SOFT]]&lt;br&gt;[[WP:SOW]]}}
'''Wikipedia''' mainly runs on [[MediaWiki]], the [[wiki]] platform written in [[PHP]], and there are a number of customized modifications of the wiki, built for other [[WikiMedia]] projects, or for external projects. (See [[Wikipedia:MediaWiki]])
hello

There have also been scripts written specifically for working with Wikpedia as well as with other MediaWiki-based sites, such as &quot;wiki format&quot; scripts for text editors, bots, extensions for browsers, and site tools that help with particular aspects of editing Wikipedia.

== Wiki server-side software ==
* [[MediaWiki]] - Wikipedia flagship software
* [[WikiTeX]] - extension package for MediaWiki published as a complete package.

==CSS extensions ==
* [[User:Taka/Tooltips]] - in browser hover [[tooltip]] code 
* [[Help:User style]] - on personalized CSS editing.

==Browser extensions==
''See also [[Wikipedia:Toolbars]].''
*[[Extension (Mozilla)]]
**[http://wikipedia.mozdev.org http://wikipedia.mozdev.org] - Firefox (Mozilla?) plug-in for [[toolbar]] for editing Wikipedia or any other MediaWiki site (with configuration).
**[https://addons.mozilla.org/extensions/moreinfo.php?id=394 https://addons.mozilla.org/extensions/moreinfo.php?id=394]- the ViewSourceWith extension for Firefox. Allows one to open up an edit box in an external editor (like emacs or vim) and automatically update any changes made and saved.

==Text editor extensions/plugins ==
* [[Vim (text editor)|Vim]] - Wikipedia format highlighting script
* [[Kate (editor)]] - Wikipedia format highlighting script
* [[Wikipedia:Wikipedia-mode.el|Wikipedia-mode.el]] - [[User:CYD]]'s [[Emacs]] major mode for editing Wikipedia articles offline.

== Bots/Scripts ==
* [[Wikipedia:Table converters]] for web-based table converters

==See also==
*[[Wikipedia:Scripts]]
*[[Wikipedia:Tools]]

[[pt:Wikipedia:Software]]</text>
