'''Pomacentridae''' ([[New Latin]], from [[Greek language|Greek]] &quot;poma&quot; [[Operculum (Fish)|operculum]] + &quot;kentron&quot; [[Sting (biology)|sting]]) is a family of [[perciform]] fish, comprising the [[damselfish]]es and [[clownfish]]es.  They are exclusively [[ocean|marine]] (rarely [[brackish]]), and noted for their hardy constitutions and [[territoriality]].  Many are brightly coloured, so they are popular in [[aquarium|aquaria]].

Around 360 [[species]] are classified in this family, in approximately 28 [[genus|genera]].  Of these, members of two genera, ''Amphiprion'' and  ''Premnas'' are commonly called [[Clownfish]] or '''Anemonefish''', while members of other genera (e.g. ''Chromis'') are commonly called '''Damselfish'''.

{{fish-stub}}

