    <title>Corned beef knot</title>
    <id>176404</id>
    <revision>
      <id>16062233</id>
      <timestamp>2005-06-08T05:27:31Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Deridolus</username>
        <id>223773</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <text xml:space="preserve">[[Image:Corned Beef &amp; Salt Pork Knot.png|thumb|200px|left|diagram on how to bind this knot]]
The '''corned beef knot''' is a [[binding knot]] usually used on smaller line. It gains its name from being used often to tie the meat of the same name while it is being cooked, as the knot has to be tightened several times before giving the final bend due to the meat's tendency to shrink while being cooked.

==External link==
* http://www.geocities.com/roo_two/butcherknots.html

{{knot-stub}}

[[Category:Knots]]</text>
