    <title>Packer's knot</title>
    <id>176405</id>
    <revision>
      <id>16062234</id>
      <timestamp>2005-04-17T01:38:19Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Mathbot</username>
        <id>234358</id>
      </contributor>
      <comment>&quot;Removed extra blank lines.&quot;</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">[[Image:Packers knot.png|thumb|200px|left|diagram of how to bind a Packers knot]]
The '''Packer's Knot''' is a binding [[knot]] usually used in smaller line.
This knot is sometimes used in baling and in parcel tying and is perhaps the most practical of Boned and Rolled Roast Knots

==External link==

*[http://www.geocities.com/roo_two/butcherknots.html diagram of a Packer's Knot]

