      <text xml:space="preserve">'''ORWO''' is a manufacturer of [[photographic film]]. The basis for ORWO was the [[Agfa-Gevaert|AGFA]] [[Wolfen]] plant, which was located in what was to become [[East Germany]], and thus nationalized after [[World War II|WWII]].

The ORWO trademark (for ''Original Wolfen'') was introduced in [[1964]].

