[[Category:Executed people|Czolgosz, Leon]]
[[Category:History of Cleveland|Czolgosz, Leon]]

[[de:Leon Czolgosz]]
[[nl:Leon Czolgosz]]
[[pl:Leon Czolgosz]]</text>
    </revision>
  </page>
  <page>
    <title>Miroku (InuYasha)</title>
    <id>176462</id>
    <revision>
      <id>42150951</id>
      <timestamp>2006-03-04T03:51:47Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Linkdude20002001</username>
        <id>599661</id>
      </contributor>
      <comment>Kazāna</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">{{IY Character|
Name=Miroku|
ImageName=Miroku Manga.jpg|
JapaneseName=弥勒|
RomajiName=Miroku|
AlternateName=|
Age=18|
Race=Human|
Weapon=Kazāna, Staff, Spell Scrolls|
FamConnect=&lt;li&gt;Father ''(deceased)''&lt;li&gt;Mushin ''(foster father)''|
}}

:''This article is about a character from an anime series; see [[Maitreya]] for the future Buddha known as Miroku in Japanese''

'''Miroku''' (&amp;#24357;&amp;#21202;) is a fictional character in the [[anime]] and [[manga]] series ''[[InuYasha]]''.

He is a [[Buddhism|Buddhist]] monk, called ''h&amp;#333;shi'' (&amp;#27861;&amp;#24107;) in [[Japanese language|Japanese]], who possesses a rather unusual [[curse]]. His right hand has a slowly expanding &quot;Kazāna&quot; that sucks in anything nearby if it's not kept covered by a cloth and strand of [[mala]] beads. This curse was placed on Miroku's grandfather by [[Naraku]] and passed down to him. Eventually, the curse will cause him to be sucked in as well, unless Naraku is defeated. 

Miroku meets [[Inuyasha (character)|Inuyasha]] and his friends while walking away from a town after cheating a rich man there out of some money. He discovers that [[Kagome Higurashi|Kagome]] has shards of the [[Shikon no Tama]] (The Jewel of the Four Souls) and takes them and her bike with the help of his [[tanuki]] (raccoon dog spirit) friend, [[Hachiemon|Hachi]]. Inuyasha and Kagome catch up to him and Inuyasha attacks him, but Miroku uses his Kazāna in return. Kagome, realizing that the monk will not harm humans, stands in its path and causes Miroku to quickly cover it with his prayer beads. Miroku explains his situation, and Inuyasha reluctantly allows him to join them.

Despite his good looks and tempermant, Miroku's worst vice (and best running joke) is lechery, specifically shameless flattery and occasional groping with varying subtlety. Miroku apparently feels that he must have a child in order to have an heir by the time he may be killed by the curse, and thus finds it perfectly fine to offer the chance for someone to bear his child. This later puts some strain on his blossoming relationship (eventually a marriage proposal) with Sango, often ruining small romantic moods between them.

Nonetheless, the monk mellows out as time goes on and proves to be a very valuable--if perverted--ally. He is very knowledgeable about [[Yokai|yōkai]], and is the primary fighter of the team after Inuyasha. Though quite possibly the most intelligent one of the group, he often uses humor or lechery to lighten serious situations, especially if anyone is worried about him. Despite his lighthearted and lecherous exterior, it is clear he has an inner darkness (Shippō has been heard to comment that he 'never bought that holy man routine') and worries over his curse and the death sentence that hangs over his head from it.

[[Image:Miroku.gif|thumb|left| Miroku as portrayed in the anime series]]

==Name==
* The character is named for the predicted [[Buddha]] of the future, [[Maitreya]], who is called Miroku in Japanese.

==Voice Actor==
*[[Japan|Japanese]] [[Seiyū]]: [[Kouji Tsujitani]]
*English Voice Actor: [[Kirby Morrow]]
*Brazilian Voice Actor: [[Fábio Lucindo]]
*Spanish Voice Actor: [[Gabriel Gama]]

==Friends==
*[[Hachiemon]] - His partner-in-crime before Miroku met Inuyasha and friends. This [[tanuki]] (raccoon dog) [[juujin|j&amp;#363;jin]] would act as a [[yokai|y&amp;#333;kai]] and the sneaky monk would pretend to drive him off. The hōshi would then collect from the y&amp;#333;kai's &quot;victims.&quot;  Hachi is very loyal to Miroku, though sometimes he would use his shape-shifting abilities to his own advantage and pose as Miroku to 'cast out yōkai' in exchange for food and other necessities, but their friendship is very solid. Due to Hachi's friendly nature, he is very polite and congenial to others.
*[[Inuyasha (character)|Inuyasha]] - Inuyasha may not like how the monk does things, but he does respect the monk for his good skills, talents, and his knowledge of [[yokai|y&amp;#333;kai]]. They have saved each other's lives several times, and both know that they can trust the other to help if there is a need.
*[[Shippō]] - The critical [[kitsune]] disapproves of the monk's methods, but he also recognizes a good ally.
*[[Kagome Higurashi]] - They don't really interact very much. He seems more interested in Sango. Though when he first joined the group he asked Kagome if she would bear his child -- like he asks every girl.
*[[Sango (Inuyasha)|Sango]] - He restrains himself out of sympathy at first, but becomes his lecherous self after she recovers. He acts especially perverted around her when he is injured and she is in a convenient spot. As the story progresses, it becomes clearer that he is in love with her. In a much later episode, he actually asks her to marry him once Naraku is defeated. If fact he does not ask her to marry him, he asks her to live with him and bare him 20 children. Interestingly, despite Miroku's continuous questioning of pretty girls to bear his child, he never asked Sango this question until she brought it up in a fit of jealousy.

==Powers and Attacks==
*'''Kazāna''' ([[Japanese]]: '''風穴''', [[Hiragana]]: '''かざあな''', [[English]]: '''Wind Tunnel''': Acts as a mini-[[black hole]] that can suck anything in. Miroku's grandfather was cursed by Naraku with the Hole in his right hand, and it has passed on to his father and now him. If Naraku is not destroyed in time, Miroku will be drawn in sharing the fate of his father and grandfather. One advantage of this curse is that it gives Miroku a deadly weapon which puts him on level ground with hordes of yōkai. There are a few weaknesses of this attack, such as Naraku's hell wasps called the Saimy&amp;#333;sh&amp;#333;, which will kill Miroku with their poison if an excess number of them are drawn in, and anything that may expand the hole (a knife, etc.) and cause the curse to spread faster. The Saimy&amp;#333;sh&amp;#333; have been near to killing him several times as Miroku seems determined to rather die of the poison than let his friends be harmed.
*Superspeed: In short bursts, Miroku can run swiftly enough to keep pace with Inuyasha; even if carrying extra weight (i.e., another person) on his back. Whether this speed is granted by spell or by innate ability is unclear.
*Spell Scrolls (&amp;#26413; ''fuda''): Can be used to paralyze y&amp;#333;kai and create barriers. Most are thrown and then bind to the y&amp;#333;kai. See also: [[O-fuda]]
*Invisibility: Miroku can mask objects (both living and inanimate) from the eyes of evildoers, by going into a state of intense meditation.
*Force Field (&amp;#32080;&amp;#30028; ''kekkai''): With the assistance of his staff, Miroku can create and temporarily sustain small protective force fields of reasonable strength.
*Staff: Miroku's staff, known as a Shakujo, is a wooden staff with a circular golden charm on the top. The charm is a circle with a pattern through the center of spheres and double crescents. On each side of the circle, there are three thin gold rings. Even though his Kazāna and holy abilities are very powerful, Miroku is shown to be a formidable opponent when using the staff.
*Pervertness - Miroku's hands are &quot;cursed&quot; to keep rubbing women's butts. (at least he says they're &quot;cursed&quot;)

{{InuyashaCharacter}}
[[Category:Fictional Buddhists]]

[[es:Miroku]]
[[ru:&amp;#1052;&amp;#1080;&amp;#1088;&amp;#1086;&amp;#1082;&amp;#1091;]]</text>
